1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,600
One PhyGenBench example: the Cosmos baseline,
and Cosmos with our full Physis-Lang pipeline.

2
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:09,200
Watch how the butter melts.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,600
A conventional caption only names the event.

4
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:18,000
Physical language makes the process explicit:

5
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:22,000
the cause, the governing law,
and the resulting effect.

6
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,700
We refine shared guidelines,
not individual captions.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:29,900
First, one guideline instructs
a fixed captioner across videos.

8
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:37,100
A physics-aware critic checks each description
for correctness and coverage.

9
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:42,200
An agent turns recurring errors
into a better shared instruction.

10
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:47,400
Each version is validated on PhysCapBench
until gains saturate.

11
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:50,600
Caption quality improves.

12
00:00:50,900 --> 00:00:55,500
With Cosmos kept fixed, the same guideline
versions also improve video generation.

13
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:00,500
Physical language also selects training data:

14
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:05,100
model deficiencies become physics tags,
matched as text against gallery captions.

15
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:08,200
Matching videos are retrieved and recaptioned.

16
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,500
Compared with WISA alone,
adding the retrieved videos

17
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:15,300
improves all three benchmarks,
by about three points on average.

18
00:01:17,700 --> 00:01:22,400
On four physical benchmarks, Physis-Lang
improves over the Cosmos3-Nano baseline.

19
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:30,700
The gains carry across backbones and scales:

20
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:35,100
mean improvements range
from three to seven points.

21
00:01:37,900 --> 00:01:42,200
Models trained with Physis-Lang generate
videos with coherent physical dynamics.

22
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:58,800
Represent physics in language, evolve shared
guidelines, and target data expansion.

23
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:03,000
Physical language connects
representation, refinement, and data.
